%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 2cbb47ee54ad14dddab18d7873dc4523, type: 3}
  m_Name: LC_Main
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: BugReport.Runtime::BugReport.Progress.LevelCatalog
  levels:
  - id: training_lab
    sceneName: Level_01_TrainingLab
    title: TRAINING LAB
    chapter: '1: HELLO, WORLD'
    parUses: 6
    chapterIndex: 1
    intro: 
    outro: 'The knight reached the exit and has no idea anything happened. The system files a note: ANOMALY, LOW PRIORITY.'
  - id: bridge_out
    sceneName: Level_02_BridgeOut
    title: BRIDGE OUT
    chapter: '1: HELLO, WORLD'
    parUses: 1
    chapterIndex: 1
    intro: The bridge is a hologram. The old barrier is solid. Solidity is just a setting.
    outro: 'Cross-referencing: ''bridge'' now has collision. Cause unknown.'
  - id: two_doors
    sceneName: Level_03_TwoDoors
    title: TWO DOORS, ONE SHADOW
    chapter: '1: HELLO, WORLD'
    parUses: 2
    chapterIndex: 1
    intro: Two firewalls, one shadow. If a power is in use, [R] undoes it and gives the object back.
    outro: Firewall breach logged twice. Both marked 'resolved'. Neither was.
  - id: two_birds
    sceneName: Level_04_TwoBirds
    title: TWO BIRDS
    chapter: '1: HELLO, WORLD'
    parUses: 1
    chapterIndex: 1
    intro: One transfer can fix two problems, if you think about where the solidity lands.
    outro: The designers will notice that one. They won't understand it.
  - id: fork_in_the_road
    sceneName: Level_21_ForkInTheRoad
    title: FORK IN THE ROAD
    chapter: '1: HELLO, WORLD'
    parUses: 1
    chapterIndex: 1
    intro: Two roads. The knight takes the shortest one that is open. You decide which one that is.
    outro: He never noticed there was a choice.
  - id: three_plates
    sceneName: Level_05_ThreePlates
    title: THREE PLATES
    chapter: '2: DUPLICATE OBJECTIVE'
    parUses: 2
    chapterIndex: 2
    intro: Three plates, one crate. The game never said you only get one.
    outro: 'ITEM COUNT: +2. Nobody authorised that.'
  - id: copy_the_copy
    sceneName: Level_06_CopyTheCopy
    title: COPY THE COPY
    chapter: '2: DUPLICATE OBJECTIVE'
    parUses: 2
    chapterIndex: 2
    intro: A copy is a crate like any other. It can be copied too.
    outro: Duplicates of duplicates. The inventory system has stopped counting.
  - id: stop_the_platform
    sceneName: Level_07_StopThePlatform
    title: STOP THE PLATFORM
    chapter: '3: TIME DOES NOT APPLY'
    parUses: 1
    chapterIndex: 3
    intro: Time is just another rule. Pause the platform; the knight will take it from there.
    outro: Timer anomaly detected. Timer anomaly ignored.
  - id: two_pistons
    sceneName: Level_08_TwoPistons
    title: TWO PISTONS
    chapter: '3: TIME DOES NOT APPLY'
    parUses: 2
    chapterIndex: 3
    intro: A freeze does not last forever. Spend them one at a time.
    outro: The pistons were never meant to stop. Neither was he.
  - id: the_build
    sceneName: Level_09_TheBuild
    title: THE BUILD
    chapter: '3: TIME DOES NOT APPLY'
    parUses: 3
    chapterIndex: 3
    intro: A bit of everything you have learned so far. A recap, and a rehearsal.
    outro: Build 1.0 passed internal testing. Your fingerprints are all over it.
  - id: heavy_lifting
    sceneName: Level_10_HeavyLifting
    title: HEAVY LIFTING
    chapter: '4: DEAD WEIGHT'
    parUses: 1
    chapterIndex: 4
    intro: The system is checking weights now. A number is just a number.
    outro: 'MASS ERROR: crate = 60 kg. Cannot reproduce.'
  - id: twin_scales
    sceneName: Level_11_TwinScales
    title: TWIN SCALES
    chapter: '4: DEAD WEIGHT'
    parUses: 3
    chapterIndex: 4
    intro: Two plates, two heavy demands. You have the tools to meet both.
    outro: Scales calibrated. Probably.
  - id: weigh_station
    sceneName: Level_12_WeighStation
    title: WEIGH STATION
    chapter: '4: DEAD WEIGHT'
    parUses: 2
    chapterIndex: 4
    intro: A gate that wants weight, a pit that wants floor. Different problems, different tools.
    outro: Two systems failed on the same tick. Coincidence, says the log.
  - id: night_watch
    sceneName: Level_13_NightWatch
    title: NIGHT WATCH
    chapter: '5: NIGHT SHIFT'
    parUses: 1
    chapterIndex: 5
    intro: Security has arrived. The guard is not stupid, only easily distracted.
    outro: 'Guard reports: ''I was investigating a barrel.'''
  - id: double_shift
    sceneName: Level_14_DoubleShift
    title: DOUBLE SHIFT
    chapter: '5: NIGHT SHIFT'
    parUses: 2
    chapterIndex: 5
    intro: Two guards, one decoy, fourteen seconds. Be patient.
    outro: Both guards were later found near the same barrel.
  - id: frozen_stiff
    sceneName: Level_15_FrozenStiff
    title: FROZEN STIFF
    chapter: '5: NIGHT SHIFT'
    parUses: 2
    chapterIndex: 5
    intro: A guard and a piston. Different problems; you know which glitch fits which.
    outro: Staff morale is low. Maintenance is lower.
  - id: false_wall
    sceneName: Level_16_FalseWall
    title: FALSE WALL
    chapter: '6: FALSE FLOORS'
    parUses: 1
    chapterIndex: 6
    intro: The system is losing track of what is where. A wall can be somewhere else than it looks.
    outro: Collision and visuals disagree. Please do not tell anyone.
  - id: false_floor
    sceneName: Level_17_FalseFloor
    title: FALSE FLOOR
    chapter: '6: FALSE FLOORS'
    parUses: 1
    chapterIndex: 6
    intro: The same trick builds as well as breaks. Slide a floor where it is needed.
    outro: A floor has been found in a pit. Investigating.
  - id: searchlight
    sceneName: Level_18_Searchlight
    title: SEARCHLIGHT
    chapter: '6: FALSE FLOORS'
    parUses: 2
    chapterIndex: 6
    intro: The system sends a drone. Anything in its light is reported. Mind your containment.
    outro: 'Drone report: ''I saw nothing. I saw it very clearly.'''
  - id: stack_the_order
    sceneName: Level_19_StackTheOrder
    title: STACK THE ORDER
    chapter: '6: FALSE FLOORS'
    parUses: 2
    chapterIndex: 6
    intro: The system is on edge today. Whatever you break first, it fixes first.
    outro: 'Patch notes: ''Fixed a crate.'' The bridge was not mentioned.'
  - id: report_closed
    sceneName: Level_20_ReportClosed
    title: REPORT CLOSED
    chapter: '7: REPORT CLOSED'
    parUses: 5
    chapterIndex: 7
    intro: The last room. Every rule you learned, in order. Close the report.
    outro: 'BUG REPORT #1: CLOSED. Resolution: ''works as intended''. The knight walks home. You stay in the game.'
